WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:04.030 --> 00:00:07.110
This scene here is very
high-tech. [laughs]

00:00:07.110 --> 00:00:09.187
There are guys in the military,

00:00:09.187 --> 00:00:10.545
certain groups around the world

00:00:10.545 --> 00:00:12.578
that can absolutely do this.

00:00:12.578 --> 00:00:14.733
Hi, I'm Cain Vincent Dyer.

00:00:14.733 --> 00:00:17.770
I committed over 100 bank robberies

00:00:17.770 --> 00:00:20.760
in a period of almost two years.

00:00:20.760 --> 00:00:22.651
After turning myself in,

00:00:22.651 --> 00:00:26.559
I decided to form a coaching company

00:00:26.559 --> 00:00:28.720
that helps people transform their lives.

00:00:28.720 --> 00:00:32.090
And today we are going to be judging

00:00:32.090 --> 00:00:35.300
the authenticity of bank-robbery scenes

00:00:35.300 --> 00:00:37.033
in some of our favorite movies.

00:00:43.430 --> 00:00:44.913
He has on this helmet,

00:00:44.913 --> 00:00:46.746
so he doesn't need a mask.

00:00:46.746 --> 00:00:50.345
He doesn't look like he'd be
coming in to rob, necessarily.

00:00:50.345 --> 00:00:51.930
It looks like he just kept his helmet on,

00:00:51.930 --> 00:00:53.530
which guys do all the time.

00:00:55.730 --> 00:00:58.410
I can really, really relate to this,

00:00:58.410 --> 00:01:00.120
him wearing that backpack.

00:01:00.120 --> 00:01:02.240
I would sometimes either wear a backpack

00:01:02.240 --> 00:01:05.340
or a duffel bag strapped around the front,

00:01:05.340 --> 00:01:07.610
and you can still have
the control of your hands.

00:01:07.610 --> 00:01:08.685
That's the only drawback --

00:01:08.685 --> 00:01:11.635
if you get any kind of
tracker or dye pack,

00:01:11.635 --> 00:01:14.490
you walk off, and that dye pack explodes,

00:01:14.490 --> 00:01:16.032
he's wearing it on his chest.

00:01:17.180 --> 00:01:18.405
Luke: Fuck.

00:01:20.019 --> 00:01:22.080
This is so real.

00:01:22.080 --> 00:01:25.100
It typically happens
your first time or two.

00:01:25.100 --> 00:01:27.391
Bank robbery is bad enough, so,

00:01:27.391 --> 00:01:28.941
just to put that out there.

00:01:28.941 --> 00:01:31.170
What we know from watching the movie

00:01:31.170 --> 00:01:33.650
is he's in a really desperate situation.

00:01:33.650 --> 00:01:35.616
Sometimes the desperation kind of

00:01:35.616 --> 00:01:37.991
overrides the moral compass.

00:01:37.991 --> 00:01:39.381
It's very accurate.

00:01:39.381 --> 00:01:41.997
It takes a second for
him to pump himself up.

00:01:42.997 --> 00:01:44.260
Luke: You! Get up!

00:01:44.260 --> 00:01:45.835
He has tape.

00:01:45.835 --> 00:01:48.130
He doesn't want those gloves coming off.

00:01:48.130 --> 00:01:50.522
So obviously he's really conscious

00:01:50.522 --> 00:01:53.055
of not leaving any type of fingerprints.

00:01:53.055 --> 00:01:57.464
Also, it's holding his
sleeve to the jacket down,

00:01:57.464 --> 00:02:01.670
which could be covering
up some type of tattoo.

00:02:01.670 --> 00:02:04.573
Interesting that he
picked a bank with glass.

00:02:04.573 --> 00:02:08.020
Because of the glass, he's
got to throw it over to them,

00:02:08.020 --> 00:02:09.361
and, you know, they could put

00:02:09.361 --> 00:02:10.952
any kind of device in that bag.

00:02:10.952 --> 00:02:14.690
It almost shows more so the desperation,

00:02:14.690 --> 00:02:17.360
that he went into this
bank that is secure,

00:02:17.360 --> 00:02:19.222
with glass and everything like that,

00:02:19.222 --> 00:02:23.395
but he was still so desperate
that it didn't stop him.

00:02:23.395 --> 00:02:24.769
[motorcycle engine sputtering]

00:02:24.769 --> 00:02:25.760
Son of a --

00:02:26.633 --> 00:02:28.937
Him having a problem with his motorcycle

00:02:28.937 --> 00:02:31.033
is something -- sure, it's happened.

00:02:31.033 --> 00:02:35.070
[police sirens blaring]
[tires squealing]

00:02:35.070 --> 00:02:36.957
They just blow through that red light

00:02:36.957 --> 00:02:38.982
with all those cars coming.

00:02:38.982 --> 00:02:41.765
I don't think a

00:02:41.765 --> 00:02:44.072
intelligent police officer would do that,

00:02:44.072 --> 00:02:47.147
just because you're putting
a lot more people at risk.

00:02:47.147 --> 00:02:49.662
I would actually rate this

00:02:49.662 --> 00:02:50.740
a 9.

00:02:50.740 --> 00:02:53.370
Going into the bank,
leading up to the bank,

00:02:53.370 --> 00:02:56.400
preparing, getting nervous
-- everything he did,

00:02:56.400 --> 00:03:00.159
even the mistakes he made inside,

00:03:00.159 --> 00:03:03.767
were actual mistakes that
if you haven't done it,

00:03:03.767 --> 00:03:05.076
you would probably make.

00:03:08.690 --> 00:03:11.760
This vault that looks like
no one could ever get in

00:03:11.760 --> 00:03:14.000
except for probably the US military.

00:03:14.000 --> 00:03:17.620
We have to keep in mind that, this movie,

00:03:17.620 --> 00:03:18.928
everything about this movie

00:03:18.928 --> 00:03:20.836
is supposed to be over the top.

00:03:20.836 --> 00:03:24.849
Yes, they do have very
intricate lock safes

00:03:24.849 --> 00:03:27.025
and things like that, timed lock safes,

00:03:27.025 --> 00:03:29.290
things that are really hard to get into.

00:03:29.290 --> 00:03:32.834
But a lot of time, during business hours,

00:03:32.834 --> 00:03:36.484
they will keep certain safes open

00:03:36.484 --> 00:03:39.105
just so the employees can have access.

00:03:39.105 --> 00:03:41.054
I learned everything.

00:03:41.054 --> 00:03:43.745
So, at every bank I went into,

00:03:43.745 --> 00:03:46.581
I knew whether it was going to have a safe

00:03:46.581 --> 00:03:49.769
such as the one that's in this scene

00:03:49.769 --> 00:03:52.894
or if it was going to be, say,

00:03:52.894 --> 00:03:55.052
regular open doors.

00:03:55.052 --> 00:03:58.570
And if it were like this,
I would pass. [laughs]

00:03:58.570 --> 00:04:01.745
Unless I found in one of their manuals

00:04:01.745 --> 00:04:04.537
or knew that they would
keep this door open

00:04:04.537 --> 00:04:06.612
between certain times.

00:04:06.612 --> 00:04:08.510
Could I get into that?

00:04:08.510 --> 00:04:12.730
Back then, where things
were more manual, oh, yeah.

00:04:12.730 --> 00:04:15.988
I mean, it would've taken

00:04:15.988 --> 00:04:18.040
a considerable amount of
time to break into that.

00:04:18.040 --> 00:04:20.611
That's not, like, a three-
or four-minute deal.

00:04:22.227 --> 00:04:23.408
[gunshot]

00:04:24.516 --> 00:04:25.844
[cocks gun]

00:04:25.844 --> 00:04:28.510
You wouldn't have a
weapon in there like that,

00:04:28.510 --> 00:04:30.836
unless you have a security
guard that was armed.

00:04:30.836 --> 00:04:32.910
You gotta keep in mind,
if you shoot that shotgun

00:04:32.910 --> 00:04:35.492
and he hits that bank-robbery suspect,

00:04:35.492 --> 00:04:39.250
those rounds are probably
exiting the perpetrator

00:04:39.250 --> 00:04:41.566
and going straight into the bank customer

00:04:41.566 --> 00:04:42.999
or the bank employee.

00:04:42.999 --> 00:04:44.251
Robber: What bus driver?

00:04:44.251 --> 00:04:45.870
[windows shatter]

00:04:45.870 --> 00:04:48.830
That school bus doesn't
have any damage on it,

00:04:48.830 --> 00:04:51.764
and it just crashed through

00:04:51.764 --> 00:04:54.639
a cement and stone building.

00:04:54.639 --> 00:04:55.540
And, if you remember,

00:04:55.540 --> 00:04:57.014
it had to go up the steps,

00:04:57.014 --> 00:04:58.189
because when they robbed the building

00:04:58.189 --> 00:05:00.028
they went up the steps, and that --

00:05:00.028 --> 00:05:02.620
like, totally Hollywood, right?

00:05:02.620 --> 00:05:04.831
Definitely a 1. [chuckles]

00:05:08.290 --> 00:05:12.471
The camera's already got them on video,

00:05:12.471 --> 00:05:14.522
so why even use a mask at that point?

00:05:14.522 --> 00:05:16.796
Either they should've
gotten out of the car,

00:05:16.796 --> 00:05:19.200
gone straight in with the mask on,

00:05:19.200 --> 00:05:22.180
or not used anything.

00:05:22.180 --> 00:05:25.310
Robber: Stay down! We want to hurt no one.

00:05:25.310 --> 00:05:26.985
The energy is so on point.

00:05:26.985 --> 00:05:30.025
How they talk, how they
walk, how they move.

00:05:30.025 --> 00:05:33.100
Even the customers, just
the fear that's there.

00:05:35.940 --> 00:05:39.051
Cellophane money. The
money's still wrapped.

00:05:39.051 --> 00:05:41.910
This is how a lot of
banks will keep the money

00:05:41.910 --> 00:05:43.010
when it comes in.

00:05:43.010 --> 00:05:45.501
Because they're still coming from,

00:05:45.501 --> 00:05:47.416
you know, basically the factory.

00:05:47.416 --> 00:05:50.045
Robber: Down! Down.

00:05:50.045 --> 00:05:53.980
Detective: Far East National Bank, 11:30!

00:05:53.980 --> 00:05:57.288
The silent alarm is actually going off

00:05:57.288 --> 00:05:59.238
as they're leaving,

00:05:59.238 --> 00:06:03.250
which is what employees
are actually trained to do.

00:06:03.250 --> 00:06:05.790
It's less chance of the cops getting there

00:06:05.790 --> 00:06:08.158
and them having a hostage situation.

00:06:08.158 --> 00:06:09.841
The police are being alerted

00:06:09.841 --> 00:06:11.832
as the bank robbers are leaving,

00:06:11.832 --> 00:06:14.010
which is super accurate.

00:06:14.010 --> 00:06:16.810
I would actually give it about a 7.

00:06:16.810 --> 00:06:20.080
The energy is so accurate
for the bank robbers,

00:06:20.080 --> 00:06:23.015
for that team. You can
feel the desperation

00:06:23.015 --> 00:06:24.490
that it needs to get done.

00:06:27.377 --> 00:06:28.811
Robber: Move, move, move!

00:06:28.811 --> 00:06:30.600
All right, back it away from the counter!

00:06:30.600 --> 00:06:32.415
They know exactly what they're doing.

00:06:32.415 --> 00:06:35.625
You can tell by the way
they move, where they go;

00:06:35.625 --> 00:06:38.119
they know the layout of this place.

00:06:38.119 --> 00:06:39.652
Robber: Up against the wall!

00:06:39.652 --> 00:06:41.910
You! Away from the computer!

00:06:41.910 --> 00:06:43.126
Bank robberies that are done

00:06:43.126 --> 00:06:45.613
by a lot of different gangs,

00:06:45.613 --> 00:06:46.721
this is how they go in,

00:06:46.721 --> 00:06:48.379
and this is how they operate.

00:06:48.379 --> 00:06:51.548
Just with brute force and sheer fear.

00:06:51.548 --> 00:06:53.387
Robber: When's the time lock set for?

00:06:53.387 --> 00:06:54.328
9 o'clock.

00:06:54.328 --> 00:06:56.138
Robber: Don't lie to us. It's 8:15.

00:06:56.138 --> 00:06:59.845
He asked her something very
specific about the bank

00:06:59.845 --> 00:07:01.495
which he already knew.

00:07:01.495 --> 00:07:05.328
I would ask a bank employee a question

00:07:05.328 --> 00:07:08.121
just because I knew the answer,

00:07:08.121 --> 00:07:09.090
and I wanted to see

00:07:09.090 --> 00:07:11.100
if they were gonna be
straight with me or not.

00:07:11.100 --> 00:07:13.360
I wanted to see if they
were gonna be nervous,

00:07:13.360 --> 00:07:16.103
how they were gonna respond
to the question I was asking.

00:07:16.103 --> 00:07:18.711
He just wanted to see if
she was gonna cooperate.

00:07:21.695 --> 00:07:24.460
Robber: Hold it! Silent
alarm, this address.

00:07:24.460 --> 00:07:25.293
You pull the alarm?

00:07:25.293 --> 00:07:26.370
No! No!

00:07:26.370 --> 00:07:29.293
A lot of people believe
that everyone in a bank,

00:07:29.293 --> 00:07:31.399
you know, all employees
have silent alarms.

00:07:31.399 --> 00:07:33.107
That's not accurate.

00:07:33.107 --> 00:07:36.327
There's very specific people

00:07:36.327 --> 00:07:39.893
that have the silent alarms

00:07:39.893 --> 00:07:41.384
that are allowed to push it.

00:07:41.384 --> 00:07:43.470
Robber: Bleaching up!

00:07:43.470 --> 00:07:44.550
Come on, let's go, we don't have time.

00:07:44.550 --> 00:07:48.552
Bleaching is something I
haven't seen done before.

00:07:48.552 --> 00:07:50.618
I know why he's doing it,

00:07:50.618 --> 00:07:52.643
to get rid of all type of evidence.

00:07:52.643 --> 00:07:56.168
You know, once you put bleach on anything,

00:07:56.168 --> 00:07:57.631
everything just kind of dissipates.

00:07:57.631 --> 00:08:00.539
It's just interesting to me
that they're doing that --

00:08:00.539 --> 00:08:04.770
like, the gloves, they have on
so much that covers them up.

00:08:04.770 --> 00:08:08.400
I would say this movie is a 10.

00:08:08.400 --> 00:08:12.347
For the realistic way that these guys

00:08:12.347 --> 00:08:13.939
are just that aggressive.

00:08:13.939 --> 00:08:16.497
Unfortunately, you have
a lot of guys who go in,

00:08:16.497 --> 00:08:17.730
and that's how they do it.

00:08:19.330 --> 00:08:21.621
Pills &amp; Coke: He's gonna kill us all.

00:08:21.621 --> 00:08:23.625
Unless...

00:08:23.625 --> 00:08:26.083
you can give me

00:08:26.083 --> 00:08:29.116
a giant f---ing s---wad of cash.

00:08:29.950 --> 00:08:31.410
I have a plan.

00:08:31.410 --> 00:08:34.183
I didn't start robbing banks just

00:08:34.183 --> 00:08:35.183
because I wanted money.

00:08:35.183 --> 00:08:38.499
I started robbing banks
out of desperation,

00:08:38.499 --> 00:08:41.660
in order to pay off a debt

00:08:41.660 --> 00:08:44.656
that a very dear relative to me

00:08:44.656 --> 00:08:48.133
had incurred to a criminal organization.

00:08:52.890 --> 00:08:55.170
When people do a solo robbery

00:08:55.170 --> 00:08:57.249
and they're trying not to be seen,

00:08:57.249 --> 00:08:59.921
this is exactly how
they would approach it.

00:08:59.921 --> 00:09:03.390
They would hand the teller a note.

00:09:03.390 --> 00:09:06.179
They would probably
smile at people in line.

00:09:06.179 --> 00:09:10.280
We can say he makes the
mistake of showing his face,

00:09:10.280 --> 00:09:12.430
but most guys that go in solo like that,

00:09:12.430 --> 00:09:16.211
they often do that, and they
hit these smaller banks,

00:09:16.211 --> 00:09:19.298
and they just hope that the
banks don't really link up

00:09:19.298 --> 00:09:20.750
and they won't get that much attention.

00:09:20.750 --> 00:09:23.008
But they will go in and
show their actual faces.

00:09:26.830 --> 00:09:29.150
You know, someone's like,
"Why is she moving that slow?"

00:09:29.150 --> 00:09:31.273
She's probably still processing.

00:09:31.273 --> 00:09:34.187
What they are trained
to do is try to give you

00:09:34.187 --> 00:09:36.510
money that has some
kind of detector in it,

00:09:36.510 --> 00:09:39.010
some kind of tracer or dye pack.

00:09:42.460 --> 00:09:43.901
And we see the stack.

00:09:43.901 --> 00:09:46.709
That stack looks a lot bigger

00:09:46.709 --> 00:09:49.499
and looks like something he should take.

00:09:49.499 --> 00:09:52.260
It could be what they
call the "bait money."

00:09:52.260 --> 00:09:57.260
A stack that bank employees
have put to the side,

00:09:57.260 --> 00:10:01.750
and with those are the bait
money, dye packs, tracers.

00:10:01.750 --> 00:10:05.430
Here we see him being captured on video.

00:10:05.430 --> 00:10:07.510
So, when I did all of my bank robberies,

00:10:07.510 --> 00:10:11.980
it was in the end of '99, going into 2000.

00:10:11.980 --> 00:10:13.331
And you didn't have cameras

00:10:13.331 --> 00:10:16.760
that were as high-quality
as they have now.

00:10:16.760 --> 00:10:20.642
So these old cameras
used to be really grainy,

00:10:20.642 --> 00:10:22.305
so they would have a lot of them,

00:10:22.305 --> 00:10:25.380
but it's very common to
have the cameras coming in.

00:10:25.380 --> 00:10:27.821
There are even things along doors

00:10:27.821 --> 00:10:31.054
that will allow a witness

00:10:31.054 --> 00:10:33.060
to gather even how tall you are,

00:10:33.060 --> 00:10:35.657
and you'll see it in a
lot of stores or banks.

00:10:35.657 --> 00:10:39.600
And when someone passes it,
the employees are trained

00:10:39.600 --> 00:10:42.512
to look where he lines up on that.

00:10:42.512 --> 00:10:45.890
Absolutely a 10. Absolutely a 10.

00:10:48.400 --> 00:10:50.263
But you see the man with the briefcase?

00:10:50.263 --> 00:10:51.220
Teller: Yes.

00:10:51.220 --> 00:10:53.988
That's my partner. He has a gun in there.

00:10:53.988 --> 00:10:55.510
And if you don't do
exactly what I tell you

00:10:55.510 --> 00:10:57.200
or if you give me any
kind of a problem at all,

00:10:57.200 --> 00:10:58.308
I'm gonna look over at my partner,

00:10:58.308 --> 00:11:01.500
and he's gonna shoot your
Mr. Gwendon between the eyes.

00:11:01.500 --> 00:11:03.258
I have done that.

00:11:03.258 --> 00:11:05.791
I have gone into a bank

00:11:05.791 --> 00:11:09.610
and immediately given instructions.

00:11:09.610 --> 00:11:14.260
I've looked back at the
door from which I came in

00:11:14.260 --> 00:11:19.171
and told an imaginary accomplice there

00:11:19.171 --> 00:11:22.113
to make sure everyone
keeps their head down --

00:11:22.113 --> 00:11:23.763
not lay down or hands in the air,

00:11:23.763 --> 00:11:25.368
but they keep their head down,

00:11:25.368 --> 00:11:28.852
like, just their eyes
focused on the ground --

00:11:28.852 --> 00:11:30.570
and there was never anyone there.

00:11:30.570 --> 00:11:32.480
Take one of those big
envelopes and put as many

00:11:32.480 --> 00:11:35.213
100s, 50s, and 20s as
you can pack into it.

00:11:35.213 --> 00:11:38.738
He's disarming her fear.

00:11:38.738 --> 00:11:40.303
Literally, you know?

00:11:40.303 --> 00:11:42.566
So it's not bringing
any attention to them.

00:11:42.566 --> 00:11:45.744
That method is a very, very common method.

00:11:45.744 --> 00:11:47.190
I would say things like that.

00:11:47.190 --> 00:11:50.943
Even if I yell louder at everyone else,

00:11:50.943 --> 00:11:53.805
I would tell the person
that I was trying to get

00:11:53.805 --> 00:11:56.073
to do whatever I'm
trying to get them to do,

00:11:56.073 --> 00:11:58.323
I would be much more calm with them,

00:11:58.323 --> 00:12:00.850
versus screaming at them.

00:12:00.850 --> 00:12:04.641
The rating I'm gonna give this picture

00:12:04.641 --> 00:12:06.582
is a 10.

00:12:06.582 --> 00:12:07.800
You know, you would think he wouldn't

00:12:07.800 --> 00:12:09.404
just go into a bank like that,

00:12:09.404 --> 00:12:11.637
but people will do things like that,

00:12:11.637 --> 00:12:14.220
especially if it's a smaller bank

00:12:14.220 --> 00:12:17.275
and they think that the
news isn't gonna travel.

00:12:17.275 --> 00:12:18.450
Police radio: All available units, we have

00:12:18.450 --> 00:12:20.083
a bank 211 in progress
Nick: Shit.

00:12:20.083 --> 00:12:21.489
at the Pico Rivera Savings in --

00:12:21.489 --> 00:12:24.605
[police sirens blaring]

00:12:24.605 --> 00:12:25.813
Stop!

00:12:27.648 --> 00:12:30.508
That is super accurate,

00:12:30.508 --> 00:12:33.720
where they're trying to back
down other law enforcement.

00:12:33.720 --> 00:12:36.851
The FBI agent that was
assigned to my case,

00:12:36.851 --> 00:12:38.270
Patrick Conley,

00:12:38.270 --> 00:12:43.040
he changed how they
went after bank robbers.

00:12:43.040 --> 00:12:46.050
And a lot of times they would
just wait for bank robbers

00:12:46.050 --> 00:12:49.110
to get caught in the,
you know, after the fact.

00:12:49.110 --> 00:12:50.480
And they'd get caught
doing something else,

00:12:50.480 --> 00:12:52.230
and someone tells on someone.

00:12:52.230 --> 00:12:54.100
We've been surveilling
these guys for weeks!

00:12:54.100 --> 00:12:55.280
That's what surveillance is!

00:12:55.280 --> 00:12:57.660
They commit a crime,
and then we stop them!

00:12:57.660 --> 00:13:00.167
The police aren't working together.

00:13:00.167 --> 00:13:02.238
In my case that happened a lot too,

00:13:02.238 --> 00:13:05.246
because other officers weren't giving

00:13:05.246 --> 00:13:07.288
Special Agent Patrick Conley

00:13:07.288 --> 00:13:10.050
the information he needed,
or they just weren't

00:13:10.050 --> 00:13:12.820
used to chasing down actual bank robbers.

00:13:12.820 --> 00:13:14.211
Anytime he heard something come up,

00:13:14.211 --> 00:13:15.670
he was always there.

00:13:15.670 --> 00:13:19.069
Once that silent alarm
was hit, he'd also go.

00:13:19.069 --> 00:13:23.419
[police sirens blaring]
[tires screeching]

00:13:24.452 --> 00:13:27.756
I have never been in that situation,

00:13:27.756 --> 00:13:31.474
where I have been inside
and the cops have shown up,

00:13:31.474 --> 00:13:34.150
but I have been in the situation where,

00:13:34.150 --> 00:13:38.062
as I'm driving away, all
the cops are coming into it.

00:13:38.062 --> 00:13:41.187
The moment I saw all the cops,

00:13:41.187 --> 00:13:42.720
I rolled all the windows down

00:13:42.720 --> 00:13:44.768
and turned my music on
and started singing.

00:13:44.768 --> 00:13:46.664
I'm gonna give it a 7,

00:13:46.664 --> 00:13:50.027
because today, you know,
I think law enforcement

00:13:50.027 --> 00:13:52.943
has learned a lot by not
communicating with each other.

00:14:02.467 --> 00:14:05.470
This scene here is very
high-tech. [laughs]

00:14:05.470 --> 00:14:08.070
This isn't a normal bank robbery, right?

00:14:08.070 --> 00:14:11.047
There are guys in the military

00:14:11.047 --> 00:14:14.046
and certain groups around the world

00:14:14.046 --> 00:14:15.862
that could absolutely do this.

00:14:15.862 --> 00:14:17.227
Now, a typical bank robbery,

00:14:17.227 --> 00:14:20.660
you're working within a
certain construct of time.

00:14:20.660 --> 00:14:23.495
And trying to get in a vault like that,

00:14:23.495 --> 00:14:26.497
even if you have the
skill set to get into it,

00:14:26.497 --> 00:14:27.555
it would probably take you

00:14:27.555 --> 00:14:29.057
as long to get in that vault

00:14:29.057 --> 00:14:31.550
as the sentence you would
get for getting into it.

00:14:31.550 --> 00:14:34.008
I have gone into banks

00:14:34.008 --> 00:14:37.574
that have safe locks in vaults

00:14:37.574 --> 00:14:39.967
and time-lock vaults and stuff like that.

00:14:39.967 --> 00:14:44.960
But there is a bank in Spain
that operates in this way,

00:14:44.960 --> 00:14:47.577
where if certain parts
of it are triggered,

00:14:47.577 --> 00:14:52.252
it will flood the actual safe
which holds all the gold.

00:14:52.252 --> 00:14:54.430
I'll give it a 10 for entertainment,

00:14:54.430 --> 00:14:57.200
but I'm gonna give it a 1

00:14:57.200 --> 00:15:01.308
on the skill set

00:15:01.308 --> 00:15:03.341
that anyone would have to go do that.

00:15:07.640 --> 00:15:09.390
I've been waiting to go into a bank

00:15:09.390 --> 00:15:11.131
and I've seen a pregnant lady

00:15:11.131 --> 00:15:14.610
or an elderly person go in,

00:15:14.610 --> 00:15:19.590
and it's made me either pause or wait,

00:15:19.590 --> 00:15:23.313
because I didn't want to --

00:15:23.313 --> 00:15:26.990
you know, like I said, a lot
of people, when they do this,

00:15:26.990 --> 00:15:29.313
they're not thinking that
they're hurting the individual,

00:15:29.313 --> 00:15:30.772
they're just taking the money.

00:15:30.772 --> 00:15:34.982
You're putting a lot
of psychological damage

00:15:34.982 --> 00:15:37.881
and trauma on someone.

00:15:37.881 --> 00:15:39.772
Sometimes you don't
realize that in the moment.

00:15:41.600 --> 00:15:42.930
Just the one, Sonny!

00:15:42.930 --> 00:15:43.996
Sonny: Right!

00:15:45.840 --> 00:15:50.114
This happened in 1972 in Brooklyn.

00:15:50.114 --> 00:15:51.781
Just a horrible situation

00:15:51.781 --> 00:15:54.784
when you have this hostage situation.

00:15:54.784 --> 00:15:59.267
[emergency sirens wailing]
[tires screeching]

00:16:02.200 --> 00:16:06.400
Right now he's in serious, serious denial.

00:16:06.400 --> 00:16:09.082
I haven't been in this situation,

00:16:09.082 --> 00:16:13.021
but I remember, even
before I turned myself in,

00:16:13.021 --> 00:16:17.239
making the decision that I
wanted to turn myself in.

00:16:17.239 --> 00:16:21.520
There was just so much
back-and-forth with myself.

00:16:21.520 --> 00:16:23.510
They got me on kidnapping, armed robbery.

00:16:23.510 --> 00:16:24.804
They're gonna bury me, man!

00:16:24.804 --> 00:16:26.203
[audience cheering]

00:16:26.203 --> 00:16:28.680
Attica! Attica! Attica!

00:16:28.680 --> 00:16:30.290
Basically, he's buying time.

00:16:30.290 --> 00:16:33.670
You're working off
survival instinct here now,

00:16:33.670 --> 00:16:36.980
because he knows. He can't go anywhere,

00:16:36.980 --> 00:16:38.800
but now it's just about survival.

00:16:38.800 --> 00:16:40.350
I'm gonna give it a 10.

00:16:40.350 --> 00:16:44.180
And were there mistakes made
in the bank? Absolutely.

00:16:44.180 --> 00:16:47.190
Were there things that
a normal bank robber

00:16:47.190 --> 00:16:50.156
wouldn't do in the bank? Yes.

00:16:50.156 --> 00:16:52.947
But in this situation,

00:16:52.947 --> 00:16:56.282
all those mistakes played
into him getting caught.

00:16:59.513 --> 00:17:01.200
Robber: We have it, let's go!

00:17:01.200 --> 00:17:03.019
A lot of bank robbers,

00:17:03.019 --> 00:17:06.252
especially their first time
or something like that,

00:17:06.252 --> 00:17:09.337
out of desperation they will just take

00:17:09.337 --> 00:17:10.770
whatever they can put in,

00:17:10.770 --> 00:17:14.086
and I've heard about
bank robbers going inside

00:17:14.086 --> 00:17:15.610
and forgetting to take anything

00:17:15.610 --> 00:17:17.618
to collect the money with, you know?

00:17:17.618 --> 00:17:19.340
Putting everything,
trying to put everything

00:17:19.340 --> 00:17:21.223
in a T-shirt, you know?

00:17:21.223 --> 00:17:22.546
Robber: I got this!

00:17:23.862 --> 00:17:27.199
He wasn't prepared for that,
which, it gave him pause,

00:17:27.199 --> 00:17:30.419
but then he had to jump back into his --

00:17:30.419 --> 00:17:32.920
into that zone of getting
them out of there.

00:17:32.920 --> 00:17:35.894
So I like that they kind of did that,

00:17:35.894 --> 00:17:38.370
where they give him this
human quality, like,

00:17:38.370 --> 00:17:40.345
"Whoa! I didn't expect that."

00:17:40.345 --> 00:17:41.761
'Cause he's just the driver.

00:17:43.220 --> 00:17:44.655
Robber: Look out!

00:17:44.655 --> 00:17:45.920
Ah! What the?!

00:17:45.920 --> 00:17:48.930
That's a situation that
can definitely happen.

00:17:48.930 --> 00:17:51.503
The guy who's engaging them

00:17:51.503 --> 00:17:54.403
has a Marine Corps hat on

00:17:54.403 --> 00:17:58.003
and a Marine Corps decal on his car.

00:17:58.003 --> 00:18:02.052
And that was something
that was always on my mind

00:18:02.052 --> 00:18:04.318
when going into a bank.

00:18:04.318 --> 00:18:06.251
You know, just wondering
if there's gonna be

00:18:06.251 --> 00:18:08.170
another guy in there like me.

00:18:08.170 --> 00:18:09.885
He was a Marine, like myself.

00:18:09.885 --> 00:18:11.650
It happened to me, where I had a guy

00:18:11.650 --> 00:18:15.992
who was probably former
military or something engage me,

00:18:15.992 --> 00:18:18.207
come at me, tell me to stop.

00:18:18.207 --> 00:18:20.107
And I followed the command.

00:18:20.107 --> 00:18:22.015
I know it sounds weird,
but I followed the command,

00:18:22.015 --> 00:18:25.988
because it just wasn't worth

00:18:25.988 --> 00:18:28.270
physically harming someone, for me.

00:18:28.270 --> 00:18:31.430
Just that scene there, that interaction,

00:18:31.430 --> 00:18:32.880
I would give it another 7.

00:18:32.880 --> 00:18:35.384
We saw a lot of violence happening,

00:18:35.384 --> 00:18:37.581
and it's easy from the outside to say,

00:18:37.581 --> 00:18:40.973
"OK, that wouldn't happen,"
but, heck, that happens.

00:18:44.240 --> 00:18:46.985
I've been into banks
where, during the day,

00:18:46.985 --> 00:18:48.678
you'd see working crews there,

00:18:48.678 --> 00:18:50.278
but I would think that
this would be something

00:18:50.278 --> 00:18:52.488
where you'd have working
crews like that at night.

00:18:52.488 --> 00:18:55.265
But if you had to have
them during the day,

00:18:55.265 --> 00:18:57.470
I can see how that guy can be in there.

00:18:57.470 --> 00:18:59.115
Robber: Easy...

00:18:59.115 --> 00:19:01.911
Everybody get down on
the f---ing floor, now!

00:19:01.911 --> 00:19:03.623
[patrons screaming]

00:19:03.623 --> 00:19:06.250
I never used a team like that.

00:19:06.250 --> 00:19:11.157
Sometimes people will get a
little violent, unfortunately.

00:19:11.157 --> 00:19:13.920
And a lot of guys probably think

00:19:13.920 --> 00:19:15.720
that's the way to instill fear,

00:19:15.720 --> 00:19:18.091
to get people to do what you tell them.

00:19:18.091 --> 00:19:20.770
But I'm kinda against that.

00:19:20.770 --> 00:19:22.980
Once again, we're looking at Hollywood;

00:19:22.980 --> 00:19:25.200
things would be much
more secure than that.

00:19:25.200 --> 00:19:29.090
But a lot of old banks did
just have the glass doors.

00:19:29.090 --> 00:19:33.558
Later on, in probably,
like, the early 2000s,

00:19:33.558 --> 00:19:36.139
what happened is you started to see banks

00:19:36.139 --> 00:19:39.640
incorporate this double-door mechanism.

00:19:39.640 --> 00:19:42.831
What that was actually for
is to trap bank robbers

00:19:42.831 --> 00:19:45.882
inside those first doors
that they went out of.

00:19:45.882 --> 00:19:49.624
I don't know. If a bunch
of serious, trained guys

00:19:49.624 --> 00:19:51.615
were doing something like this,

00:19:51.615 --> 00:19:53.830
this is probably the way they would do it.

00:19:53.830 --> 00:19:56.783
So I will rate it another 7.

